// expect: 18
// A PARENTHESIZED PATTERN IS READ AS A ONE-TUPLE. `(a)` in pattern position
// is the pattern `a` grouped, exactly as `(x)` in an expression is `x`, so
// each of the three forms below adds one to 5. All three refuse with
// E_TypeMismatch "Int vs (Int)" (measured 2026-09-25): the pattern parser
// builds a one-element tuple. The lambda form `((a)) => a + 1` runs, because
// its parameters are parsed as expressions first.
//
// Retires when a parenthesized single pattern is grouping
// (Hβ.resolve.reference-is-an-edge, the binder landing).
fn f((a)) = a + 1

fn main() = {
  let g = { (x) => x + 1 }
  let m = match 5 {
    (a) => a + 1,
  }
  f(5) + g(5) + m
}
